  "status_text": "On a ring of six lights, two moves always leave an even number on. First, each light counts itself and the lights two places either way. It lights up if the count is odd. Next, flip each light whose next clockwise neighbor is off and whose second clockwise neighbor is on. Update all lights together in each move. On a ring of three, the same moves preserve odd or even. On twelve, the final count is odd exactly when both alternating groups of six start odd. Lean checked all three (L-lib-652). Proofs are being checked and accepted. Recording and credit resume shortly. Nothing is lost.",
